   <caption unique="1261264">Instruction Operand Encoding</caption>
   </table>
  </operand_table>
 <longdesc><para unique="1261266">Reverses the byte order of a 32-bit or 64-bit (destination) register. This instruction is provided for converting little-endian values to big-endian format and vice versa. To swap bytes in a word value (16-bit register), use the XCHG instruction. When the BSWAP instruction references a 16&#8209;bit register, the result is undefined.</para>
  <para unique="1261267">In 64-bit mode, the instruction&#8217;s default operation size is 32 bits. Using a REX prefix in the form of REX.B permits access to additional registers (R8-R15). Using a REX prefix in the form of REX.W promotes operation to 64 bits. See the summary chart at the beginning of this section for encoding data and limits.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <programlisting>TEMP := DEST
IF 64-bit mode AND OperandSize = 64
	THEN
		DEST[7:0] := TEMP[63:56];
		DEST[15:8] := TEMP[55:48];
		DEST[23:16] := TEMP[47:40];
		DEST[31:24] := TEMP[39:32];
		DEST[39:32] := TEMP[31:24];
		DEST[47:40] := TEMP[23:16];
		DEST[55:48] := TEMP[15:8];
		DEST[63:56] := TEMP[7:0];
	ELSE
		DEST[7:0] := TEMP[31:24];
		DEST[15:8] := TEMP[23:16];
		DEST[23:16] := TEMP[15:8];
		DEST[31:24] := TEMP[7:0];
FI;</programlisting>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1261287">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Exceptions (All Operating Modes)">
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term>#UD </term>
    <listitem><para unique="1261289">If the LOCK prefix is used.</para>
     </listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
